    "language_probability": 1,
    "text": "Investigators who traced Russias imports kept finding the same first stop, Hong Kong and mainland China. Hong Kong is one of the biggest electronics trading hubs on Earth. Shipments arrive from American and European distributors, get resold to small trading companies, some registered only months earlier, and then leave again, by plane or by truck, heading north toward Russia. Some of these firms share the same tiny office, the same phone number, even the same registered address with dozens of others. Many of them exist only on paper. When one gets blacklisted, another one simply appears.",
